@startuml OverviewBackend
title Backend Overview: Application, Domain, and Infrastructure
allowmixing

' This diagram is an educational overview.
' Not every component shown is wired into the application yet.

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #D6B656

legend top
  |= Meaning |= Description |
  | **solid line** | Dependency in the current code |
  | **dashed line** | Planned call or missing wiring |
  | Arrow to interface | The caller knows the contract, not the concrete technology |
  | Dot --> | The arrow points to the component this component depends on or uses |
endlegend

package "API / Input (planned)" #F4F4F4 {
  component "REST Controller" as Controller <<not_yet_present>>
  note bottom of Controller
    Later:
    * Receive HTTP requests
    * Convert JSON to Java objects
    * Call a service method

    The controller must not contain availability rules.
    Authentication and Microsoft Entra ID integration are not
    part of the current local-development scope.
  end note
}

package "Application" #DCEEFF {
  class ReservationService {
    - reservationRepository: ReservationRepository
    --
    + ReservationService(repository)
    ~ getReservationsByVehicle(vehicle): List<Reservation>
    - reservationsOverlap(first, second): boolean
    - overlapsExistingReservations(newReservation): boolean
    + reserve(newReservation): void
  }

  note right of ReservationService
    **Responsibilities of the application layer**
    1. Load data through a repository
    2. Apply or coordinate business rules
    3. Save the result

    **Important:** The service knows only the
    ReservationRepository interface. It does not know how the
    repository stores its data.

    **Current state:** The helper methods and reserve(...) are implemented.
    Spring discovers the service and its repository dependency.
  end note
}

package "Domain" #E8F5E9 {
  class Reservation {
    - id: String
    - reservationNumber: String
    - startDateTime: LocalDateTime
    - endDateTime: LocalDateTime
    - status: ReservationStatus
    - vehicle: Vehicle
    - employee: Employee
    --
    + Reservation(...)
    + getId()
    + getReservationNumber()
    + getStartDateTime()
    + getEndDateTime()
    + getStatus()
    + getVehicle()
    + getEmployee()
  }

  class Vehicle {
    - id: String
    - make: String
    - model: String
    - seats: int
    - doors: int
    - transmission: String
    - licensePlate: String
    - payloadCapacity: double
    - cargoVolume: double
    - fuelType: FuelType
    - status: VehicleStatus
  }

  class Employee {
    - entraId: String
    - role: Role
  }

  enum ReservationStatus {
    PROVISIONAL
    CONFIRMED
    ACTIVE
    COMPLETED
    CANCELLED
  }

  enum VehicleStatus {
    AVAILABLE
    RENTED
    MAINTENANCE
  }

  enum FuelType {
    PETROL
    DIESEL
    ELECTRIC
    HYBRID
  }

  enum Role {
    EMPLOYEE
    ADMIN
  }

  interface ReservationRepository {
    + save(reservation): void
    + findById(id): Reservation
    + findByEmployee(employee): List<Reservation>
    + findByVehicle(vehicle): List<Reservation>
  }

  interface VehicleRepository {
    + save(vehicle): void
    + findById(id): Vehicle
    + findAll(): List<Vehicle>
    + delete(vehicle): void
  }

  interface EmployeeRepository {
    + save(employee): void
    + findByEntraId(entraId): Employee
  }

  Reservation "*" --> "1" Vehicle : reserves
  Reservation "*" --> "1" Employee : reserved by
  Reservation --> ReservationStatus

  note as DomainNote
    **Domain = "What is true and important in this business area?"**

    Contains:
    * Domain objects such as Vehicle, Employee, and Reservation
    * Domain types such as ReservationStatus
    * Repository interfaces as required contracts

    Does NOT contain:
    * HTTP, JSON, or controllers
    * A HashMap as a database
    * Dataverse-specific code

    The interfaces are intentionally located in the domain package
    so that Application and Domain know only the required contract,
    not its technical implementation.
  end note
}

package "Infrastructure" #FFF2CC {
  class InMemoryReservationRepository {
    - reservations: HashMap<String, Reservation>
    + save(reservation): void
    + findById(id): Reservation
    + findByVehicle(vehicle): List<Reservation>
    + findByEmployee(employee): List<Reservation>
  }

  class InMemoryVehicleRepository {
    - vehicles: HashMap<String, Vehicle>
    + save(vehicle): void
    + findById(id): Vehicle
    + findAll(): List<Vehicle>
    + delete(vehicle): void
  }

  class InMemoryEmployeeRepository {
    - employeesByEntraId: HashMap<String, Employee>
    + save(employee): void
    + findByEntraId(entraId): Employee
  }

  note as InfrastructureNote
    **Infrastructure = "How is a contract fulfilled technically?"**

    InMemoryReservationRepository is currently a simple
    implementation using a HashMap. Local persistence with an
    H2 database is planned; its repository implementation has
    not been added yet.

    The HashMap exists only for each repository instance.
    Its data is lost when the application restarts.
  end note
}

Controller ..> ReservationService : calls later
ReservationService --> ReservationRepository : requires contract
ReservationService --> Reservation : processes
InMemoryReservationRepository ..|> ReservationRepository : implements
InMemoryVehicleRepository ..|> VehicleRepository : implements
InMemoryEmployeeRepository ..|> EmployeeRepository : implements

note as DependencyInversion
  **Dependency Inversion / inward dependency**

  The service says: "I need some ReservationRepository."
  Spring injects the registered InMemoryReservationRepository
  into the service.

  Service constructor:
  public ReservationService(ReservationRepository repository)

  This is Dependency Injection: the concrete dependency is
  provided from outside. The service does not construct it with
  "new InMemoryReservationRepository()".

  This wiring is currently implemented with Spring.
end note

DependencyInversion .. ReservationService

